  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Wayne Earl Dahl studied at Bemidji State and the University of Minnesota before earning a doctorate in chiropractic from Logan University. He built North Metro Spine Care Specialists in Fridley, Minnesota, treating patients while also renting clinical space and providing billing and scheduling services to other chiropractors. The model extended his work beyond an individual practice into shared healthcare operations.\n\nDahl also owned SUMA MRI, a diagnostic-imaging clinic offering magnetic-resonance and radiology services. His business interests included commercial property near his clinics and ventures in Florida, where he used his chiropractic credential in a corporate role. He remained closely associated with both healthcare businesses and was remembered for his interest in animals, boats and imported classic cars.",
    "html": "<p>Wayne Earl Dahl studied at Bemidji State and the University of Minnesota before earning a doctorate in chiropractic from Logan University. He built North Metro Spine Care Specialists in Fridley, Minnesota, treating patients while also renting clinical space and providing billing and scheduling services to other chiropractors. The model extended his work beyond an individual practice into shared healthcare operations.</p>\r\n<p>Dahl also owned SUMA MRI, a diagnostic-imaging clinic offering magnetic-resonance and radiology services. His business interests included commercial property near his clinics and ventures in Florida, where he used his chiropractic credential in a corporate role. He remained closely associated with both healthcare businesses and was remembered for his interest in animals, boats and imported classic cars.</p>\r\n",
